          "figure_id": "microorganisms-14-00070-f001",
          "general_description": "Composite clinical-course figure: a labelled hospital-day timeline with probiotic, micafungin and fluconazole treatment arrows above a red line chart of C-reactive protein.",
          "detailed_description": "Top: a horizontal blue timeline with grey tick marks and a dashed break at the far left. Printed markers with boxed event labels read, left to right: \"25 days prior to admission\" Restart probiotics; HD 0 Admission; HD 2 Clostridioides difficile colitis (italic organism name); HD 10 Blood culture due to Increase of CRP; HD 15 Identification of S. cerevisiae in blood cultures; HD 19 Persistent S. cerevisiae BSI; HD 21 Removal of chemoport; HD 24 Negative blood culture; HD 42 Discharge. Below: a green arrow labelled Probiotics (25 days prior to admission - HD 15) ending at about HD 15; a blue arrow labelled Micafungin (HD 14- HD 17) starting at about HD 15; and a long orange-peach arrow labelled Fluconazole (HD 18- HD 38) extending toward HD 42. Bottom: a red line chart titled CRP with y-axis ticks 0, 10, 20, 30 and unit (mg/dL); categorical x labels Admission, HD 2, HD 10, HD 12, HD 17, HD 24, HD 31, HD 35, HD 40, Discharge. The line peaks near 27 at HD 2, falls to about 2 at HD 10, about 5 at HD 12 and about 1.5 at HD 17, then rises to about 6 at HD 24 and about 10 at HD 31, stays about 9 and 8 at HD 35 and HD 40 and ends near 2 at Discharge. Values are estimates from the plot; no data labels are printed. No patient identifiers or photographs are present.",
